1 | devops | Implement issue 66 in this repo, branch feat/per-seat-worktrees. READ FIRST the issue in full, scripts/run-remote.sh end to end (the WORK_DIR definition near line 116, the checkout block near lines 266 to 290, the guardrails install, the log collection, and how PROGRESS_ENV passes SEAT_REPO_DIR to the progress reader), scripts/dispatch.sh (the per-repo lock from PR 67 near the dispatch-lock markers, the handoff ledger, and how branches are reported at the end), the shared launcher runtime under ~/dev/agent-runtime that every dispatch overwrites in place, and docs/experience-data.md for the redaction law on paths. DELIVER, one commit per item. ONE, keep ~/dev/<repo> as the fetch point only: never check out a branch there again; before each seat, fetch origin in it. TWO, give each seat its own worktree under a per-dispatch directory (for example ~/dev/worktrees/<repo>/<dispatch id>/<task id>-<branch safe>), created with git worktree add from origin/<branch> when the branch exists on origin, else from origin/main as a new branch; run the seat in it; push from it; remove it at seat exit with git worktree remove and git worktree prune, keeping it only when the seat failed and an env var says to keep failed trees for inspection (documented). THREE, a seat that finds its branch already checked out in another live worktree of the same dispatch must wait for that seat, not fail; two seats on different branches run side by side. FOUR, the launcher runtime must not be overwritten under a running seat: ship it once per dispatch into a per-dispatch runtime directory, or ship into a versioned path and point each seat at its own copy. FIVE, the dispatch lock from PR 67 becomes a per-branch lock instead of a per-repo lock: two dispatches on the same repo run concurrently unless they touch the same branch; keep --no-wait; update the README section. SIX, the progress reader receives the worktree path as SEAT_REPO_DIR so repo-relative paths in seat_progress stay correct, and any path outside the worktree is still redacted. SEVEN, the daily worktree sweep and the sweep hook from PR 65 must also remove stale per-seat worktrees older than one day; extend scripts/worktree-sweep-install or the target repo sweep as appropriate and say which. VERIFY: bash -n on every touched script; tests/run-dispatch-lock-tests.sh and tests/run-launcher-tests.sh green; a real proof in a tmp clone with the stubbed run-remote: two seats in one wave on two branches run at the same time with two worktrees present, then both are gone at the end; two dispatches of the same repo on different branches run concurrently; two on the same branch serialize; paste the worktree list at each point and real exit codes. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Open a PR with Closes 66. Do not merge. | feat/per-seat-worktrees

